Package: pbus
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: bash (>= 5.0), coreutils (>= 8.30), util-linux, sed, grep, init-system-helpers (>= 1.51)
Suggests: libglib2.0-bin | libnotify-bin
Maintainer: pdulvp <pdulvp@laposte.net>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: system event dispatcher, an event-driven cron
 pbus runs scripts or commands when a named event is emitted. Listeners keep
 no process waiting on anything: the pbusd daemon starts them, asynchronously,
 much like a cron triggered by an event rather than by the clock.
 .
 Events and listeners are declared either through configuration files under
 /etc/pbus, or through the pbus command, which works line by line as well as
 in an interactive session.
 .
 Each event gets a key when it is created, and emitters must present it; only
 a salted hash of that key is kept on disk.
 .
 The package uses nothing beyond bash, coreutils and util-linux. The optional
 pbus-notify helper pops a desktop notification from a listener, and wants
 either gdbus or notify-send for that.
